# Consensus Reminder

For non-trivial implementation plans, use the `/consensus` command (or the bundled `consensus` skill) and launch all available `planning-buddy-*` subagents before writing code.

The same workflow applies during debugging when the proposed root cause or fix is non-obvious: draft the hypothesis, run `/consensus`, let the planning buddies challenge it from independently-modeled perspectives, and only act on the synthesized refinement.

A few minutes of cross-model scrutiny saves hours of rework — and, in debugging, prevents fixes that paper over the wrong cause.
